WEBVTT

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:12.700
[Bob] This is it. We're heading into
the final lap and McQueen

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:15.180
is right behind the leaders.
What a comeback!

00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:18.740
[Darrell] A hundred and ninety-nine
laps! It all comes down to this!

00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:20.100
This is it, kiddo.

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:22.660
You've got four turns left.
One at a time.

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:25.180
Drive it in deep and hope it sticks.

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:26.620
- Go!
- [revving]

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:30.460
We'll see about that!

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:33.580
[Bob] McQueen's going inside!

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:39.580
- Chick and King are loose!
- [Darrell] I think McQueen's out!

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:52.700
- McQueen saved it!
- [Bob] He's back on the track!

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:55.740
- Float like a Cadillac...
- Sting like a Beemer!

00:00:56.820 --> 00:01:00.460
- Ka-chow! Ka-chow! Ka...
- [all cheer]

00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:05.060
[Darrell] Lightning McQueen
is gonna win the Piston Cup!

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:07.220
Come on! You got it!
You got it, Stickers!

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:12.540
[grunts] I am not comin' in
behind you again, old man.

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:24.780
- Oh, no!
- [crowd gasps]

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:36.220
[breaks screeching]

00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:39.980
[engine idling]

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:45.460
Yeah! Whoo-hoo!

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:49.300
I won, baby! Yeah! Oh, yeah!

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:52.740
[Flo] What's he up to, Doc?

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:03.020
[grunting, moaning]

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:04.500
What are you doin', kid?

00:02:04.540 --> 00:02:07.780
I think The King
should finish his last race.

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:13.940
You just gave up the Piston Cup,
you know that?

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:17.620
This grumpy old racecar I know
once told me somethin'.

00:02:17.660 --> 00:02:19.740
It's just an empty cup.

00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:24.420
[Bob] Darrell, is pushing
on the last lap legal?

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:28.180
He's not really pushin' him. He's
just givin' him a little bump draft.

00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:30.500
Whoo-hoo-hoo-hoo-hoo!

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:33.300
Hey. What? What's goin' on?

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:35.660
- That's what I call racin'.
- [sobbing]

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:37.180
[laughing]

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:42.180
[crowd cheers wildly]

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:54.660
- Bravo il mio amico!
- Way to go, buddy!

00:02:54.700 --> 00:02:57.340
There's a lotta love out there,
you know, man?

00:02:57.380 --> 00:03:01.900
- Don't embarrass me, Fillmore.
- That's my hot rod.

00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:07.380
Come on, baby, bring it out!
Bring out the Piston Cup!

00:03:07.460 --> 00:03:08.900
Ka-chicka! Ka-chicka!

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:11.900
Yeah!
Now, that's what I'm talkin' about!

00:03:11.980 --> 00:03:15.100
Hey, how come the only one celebrating
is me, huh?

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:17.380
Where are the girls?
Bring on the confetti!

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:21.060
Ow! Ow! Easy with the confetti.
What's goin' on?

00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:24.460
Come on, snap some pictures.
I gotta go sign my deal with Dinoco!

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:25.980
Say it with me. Ka-chicka!

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:27.700
- Boo!
- Boo!

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:30.860
What's wrong with everybody?
Where's the happiness?

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:33.020
Hey! This is the start of the Chick era!

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:41.420
- Thanks, Lightnin'.
- You're welcome.

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:46.260
- Way to go, King!
- You're still the car!

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:48.340
You're The King! Yeah!

00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:51.100
[crowd cheers]

00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:58.700
[laughing and cheering]

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:02.220
- You made us proud, kid!
- Congrats on the loss, me bucko!

00:04:05.420 --> 00:04:08.060
You got a lotta stuff, kid.

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:09.940
Thanks, Doc.

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:12.420
Hey, Lightnin'.

00:04:12.460 --> 00:04:15.100
How 'bout comin' over here
and talk to me a minute?

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:19.100
Son, that was some
real racin' out there.

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:21.900
How'd you like to become
the new face of Dinoco?

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:28.100
But I didn't win.

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:31.820
Lightnin', there's a whole lot
more to racin' than just winnin'.

00:04:31.900 --> 00:04:34.580
[Clank] He was so rusty,
when he drove down the street

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:38.820
- buzzards used to circle the car!
- [all laugh]

00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:40.660
Thank you, Mr. Tex, but...

00:04:40.700 --> 00:04:44.460
...but these Rust-eze guys over there
gave me my big break.

00:04:45.980 --> 00:04:47.700
I'm gonna stick with them.

00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:50.820
Well, I sure can respect that.

00:04:50.900 --> 00:04:52.060
Still, you know,

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:55.980
if there's ever anything
I can do for you, just let me know.

00:04:56.060 --> 00:04:58.620
I sure appreciate that.
Thank you.

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:03.100
Actually, there is one thing.

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:06.020
Whoo-hoo!

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:09.980
Hey, look at me!
I'm flyin', by golly!

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:17.460
I'm happier than a tornado
in a trailer park!

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:23.380
I think it's about-a time
we redecorate.

00:05:26.540 --> 00:05:29.980
Hi. Lightning McQueen told me
this was the best place in the world

00:05:30.020 --> 00:05:31.020
to get tires.

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:35.340
How 'bout setting me and my friends up
with three or four sets each?

00:05:35.380 --> 00:05:40.580
Guido! There is a real
Michael Schumacher Ferrari in my store.

00:05:40.660 --> 00:05:42.940
A real Ferrari!

00:05:43.020 --> 00:05:45.180
Punch me, Guido.
Punch me in the face.

00:05:45.220 --> 00:05:48.700
This is the most glorious day
of my life.

00:05:50.020 --> 00:05:53.540
Wow. [Italian]
Spero che il tuo amico si riprenda.

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:55.980
Mi dicono che siete fantastici.

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:09.620
- [sighing]
- [engine revving]

00:06:09.980 --> 00:06:12.180
[both chuckle]

00:06:12.220 --> 00:06:13.780
Just passin' through?

00:06:13.860 --> 00:06:16.140
Actually, I thought I'd stop
and stay awhile.

00:06:16.220 --> 00:06:19.500
- I hear this place is back on the map.
- It is?

00:06:19.580 --> 00:06:23.340
There's some rumor floating around
that some hotshot Piston Cup racecar

00:06:23.420 --> 00:06:25.860
is setting up his big
racing headquarters here.

00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:28.740
Really? Ah, well, there goes the town.

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:31.340
You know, I really missed you, Sally.

00:06:31.420 --> 00:06:35.540
Well, I create feelings in others
they themselves don't understand and,

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:37.740
- blah, blah, blah.
- [Lightning chuckles]

00:06:38.180 --> 00:06:41.180
McQueen and Sally
parked beneath the tree,

00:06:41.260 --> 00:06:45.900
K-i-s-s-... uh... i-n-t!

00:06:46.260 --> 00:06:48.220
Great timing, Mater!

00:06:48.260 --> 00:06:52.260
Hep-non, hip-hep, hi-li-lilly! Whee!

00:06:52.380 --> 00:06:54.780
He's my best friend.
What're you gonna do?

00:06:54.860 --> 00:06:57.780
So, Stickers, last one to Flo's buys?

00:06:57.860 --> 00:07:00.580
I don't know.
Why don't we just take a drive?

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:03.260
Hmm... Nah.

00:07:04.940 --> 00:07:07.420
Yeah! Ka-chow!

00:07:07.540 --> 00:07:10.540
[♪ John Mayer: Route 66]

00:07:15.700 --> 00:07:17.820
[yelling]

